# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-19
#. type: Title #
#, no-wrap
msgid "Hamiltonian simulation {#hamiltonian-simulation}"
msgstr "Simulasi Hamiltonian {#hamiltonian-simulation}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-19
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Hamiltonian simulation is a quantum computing technique used to model and characterize quantum systems based on their energy and interactions. It has potential applications in drug discovery and chemistry, battery development, catalyst design, advanced materials, solar energy, and the study of complex physical phenomena such as superconductivity. \n"
msgstr "Simulasi Hamiltonian adalah teknik komputasi kuantum yang dipakai untuk memodelkan dan mengkarakterisasi sistem kuantum berdasarkan energi dan interaksinya. Teknik ini berpotensi diterapkan dalam penemuan obat dan kimia, pengembangan baterai, desain katalis, material canggih, energi surya, dan studi fenomena fisika kompleks seperti superkonduktivitas. \n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-19
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "By simulating molecular interactions and the behavior of electrons and atoms, Hamiltonian simulation can help researchers predict material properties, understand chemical reactions, and identify promising candidates for new technologies. Common approaches include Trotterization, which approximates continuous time evolution using sequences of quantum gates, and sample based quantum diagonalization, which estimates the energy spectrum for a given quantum system.\n"
msgstr "Dengan mensimulasikan interaksi molekul serta perilaku elektron dan atom, simulasi Hamiltonian bisa membantu peneliti memprediksi sifat material, memahami reaksi kimia, dan mengidentifikasi kandidat menjanjikan untuk teknologi baru. Pendekatan yang umum meliputi Trotterization, yang mengaproksimasi evolusi waktu kontinu menggunakan urutan Gate kuantum, dan sample based quantum diagonalization, yang mengestimasi spektrum energi untuk sistem kuantum tertentu.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-19
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "A typical workflow starts by mapping a physical system, such as a set of interacting fermions or bosons, onto qubits and circuits. From there, you can reduce the resulting circuit's depth and gate count with compilation and error-mitigation techniques, run the circuit on quantum hardware, and reconstruct the system's properties, such as its ground-state energy, from the measured samples. The tools on this page cover each of these stages, and the application functions listed here provides a single managed workflow for Hamiltonian simulation.\n"
msgstr "Alur kerja yang umum dimulai dengan memetakan sistem fisik, seperti sekumpulan fermion atau boson yang berinteraksi, ke qubit dan Circuit. Dari situ, kamu bisa mengurangi kedalaman dan jumlah Gate Circuit yang dihasilkan dengan teknik kompilasi dan mitigasi error, menjalankan Circuit di hardware kuantum, dan merekonstruksi properti sistem, seperti energi ground-state, dari sampel hasil pengukuran. Alat-alat di halaman ini mencakup setiap tahap tersebut, dan application functions yang tercantum di sini menyediakan satu managed workflow untuk simulasi Hamiltonian.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-19
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Mapping tools {#mapping-tools}"
msgstr "Alat pemetaan {#mapping-tools}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-19
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"These capabilities specialize in mapping domain problems into quantum operators and circuits for execution on a quantum computer. Use them to represent fermionic, bosonic, or spin systems, and to compile the resulting circuits so that they run with less depth and fewer entangling gates on quantum hardware.\n"
"<CardGroup>\n"
msgstr ""
"Kemampuan ini berspesialisasi dalam memetakan masalah domain ke operator dan Circuit kuantum untuk dieksekusi di komputer kuantum. Gunakan untuk merepresentasikan sistem fermionik, bosonik, atau spin, dan untuk mengompilasi Circuit yang dihasilkan agar berjalan dengan kedalaman lebih rendah dan lebih sedikit Gate entangling di hardware kuantum.\n"
"<CardGroup>\n"

