msgid "Workflow verification tools {#workflow-verification-tools}"
msgstr "Alat verifikasi alur kerja {#workflow-verification-tools}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-19
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"These tools are used for verifying workflows through classical simulation. They can simulate certain classes of circuits more efficiently than a general-purpose quantum circuit simulator. You can use them to check a workflow, such as an excitation-preserving ansatz or fermionic circuit, against a classical reference result before running it on quantum hardware.\n"
"<CardGroup>\n"
msgstr ""
"Alat-alat ini dipakai untuk memverifikasi alur kerja melalui simulasi klasik. Alat ini bisa mensimulasikan kelas Circuit tertentu dengan lebih efisien daripada simulator Circuit kuantum serba guna. Kamu bisa memakainya untuk memeriksa sebuah alur kerja, seperti ansatz excitation-preserving atau Circuit fermionik, terhadap hasil referensi klasik sebelum menjalankannya di hardware kuantum.\n"
"<CardGroup>\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-19
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"    <Card\n"
"      title=\"ffsim\"\n"
"      description=\"Simulate fermionic quantum circuits which conserve particle number and the z component of spin.\"\n"
"      href=\"https://qiskit.github.io/ffsim/\"\n"
"      analyticsName=\"Overview page: SQD\"\n"
"      linkText=\"Browse documentation\"\n"
"    />\n"
msgstr ""
"    <Card\n"
"      title=\"ffsim\"\n"
"      description=\"Simulasikan Circuit kuantum fermionik yang mempertahankan jumlah partikel dan komponen z dari spin.\"\n"
"      href=\"https://qiskit.github.io/ffsim/\"\n"
"      analyticsName=\"Overview page: SQD\"\n"
"      linkText=\"Jelajahi dokumentasi\"\n"
"    />\n"

